  "caption": "Quinn turned 60, and the low armchair suddenly felt like an opponent.\n\nMuscle strength, and especially power, tends to dip from our 50s and 60s, and that is linked with falls. The good news: muscle responds to training at any age, even in our 70s to 90s. Walking is great, but on its own it may not be enough challenge.\n\nWhat often helps: progressive resistance training two to three times a week, power work like standing up briskly from a chair, regular balance practice, and enough protein (your GP or a dietitian can advise).\n\nIf five chair stands without hands is hard, or walking or grip feels weak, a check with your GP and a physio is a good idea.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
